DOCUMENT();

loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'parserPopUp.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

Context("Numeric");
$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 0;

BEGIN_PGML

a) If [`` \lim_{x \to a} f(x) = L ``], then [`f(a) = L`].  [_]{DropDownTF(0)}

b) If [`` \lim_{x \to a} f(x) = L ``], and [`` \lim_{x \to a} g(x) = L ``]
then [`f(a)= g(a)`], [_]{DropDownTF(0)}

c) The limit [`` \lim_{x \to a} \frac{f(x)}{g(x)} ``]
  does not exist if [`g(a)=0 `], [_]{DropDownTF(0)}
END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION

The correct answers are: "False, False, False".

 You can see all the answers are false by considering:
[```h(x) = \begin{cases}
         \frac{x^2-4}{x+2} &  x \neq -2\\
         0 & x = -2\\
       \end{cases}```]

END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();

